# Source is always diffable, whatever stray bytes are in it.
#
# Git classifies a file as binary when it finds a NUL in the first 8 KiB of EITHER side of a
# diff, and then reports "Binary files differ", +0/-0 — the file becomes invisible to
# `git diff`, to the GitHub pull-request UI, and to `grep`/`rg`.
#
# That has happened three times here, from a `\x00` escape in a template literal becoming a
# real byte: `src/core/journal.ts`, `src/core/cloud/hub-registry-ops.ts`, and
# `worker/src/cursor.ts`. The last one is why this file exists rather than just a test. The
# byte was fixed, but the PRE-IMAGE at the merge base still holds it, so the diff stayed
# binary and ~1.9 KiB of net-new Worker code was unreviewable in the pull request that
# introduced it. `test/source-hygiene.test.ts` fails on a NUL in a tracked source file at HEAD
# and cannot do anything about history.
#
# `diff` here forces a textual diff regardless of content. It does not change what is stored,
# it does not normalise line endings, and it does not touch the working tree — it only tells
# git's diff machinery not to give up. Combined with the test, a stray NUL is now both refused
# going forward and harmless to review if one ever gets in again.
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.mts   diff
*.mjs   diff
*.js    diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.sql   diff
